id: pm-todos-tizu
title: "The vendored scanner passes a workflow containing an unattested publish, and the canonical one catches it"
description: "Reported by Greptile as a P1 on PR 67 and confirmed by execution rather than by reading. The chain is: a taken compound command binds a scalar, as in if true then NPM=npm fi; this copy drops the binding at the closer even though the shell retains it; the following $NPM publish is therefore never expanded and never recognised as a publish; and an attested sibling elsewhere in the file then satisfies the non-vacuity guard, so the gate reports no failures at all.\n\nMeasured with a two-step workflow whose first step publishes with --provenance and whose second publishes through the dropped binding without it. This repository's vendored scanner returns failures 0. The canonical implementation in pm-ops, called through the same auditPublishAttestation entry point on the identical input, returns failures 1 with recognition kind recognized and count 2, and names the offending command: $NPM publish is a publish path with no attested equivalent.\n\nSo the defect is in the copy, not in the design, and the canonical implementation already handles it. Checked against origin main as well: main returns failures 0 on the same input, so the pull request did not introduce this — it is pre-existing and the branch is an improvement rather than a regression.\n\nThat makes the remedy clear and it is not another patch to this copy. The two lineages have diverged to 992 lines here against 1510 in pm-ops, and every further fix applied here widens the gap while leaving the same hole in whichever copies have not been touched. pm-csv consumed the canonical gate today and deleted 443 lines of vendored scanner and 960 lines of duplicated tests doing so."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[2]: gates,security
created_at: "2026-09-03T20:08:25.424Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-03T20:08:25.424Z"
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: "This repository imports the attestation gate and shell scanner from pm-ops rather than carrying a copy; the two-step witness returns a failure naming the unattested publish, verified by executing the gate rather than by reading it; the vendored scripts and their duplicated tests are deleted rather than left beside the import; and a test asserts the gate is the resolved package export so a future hand-edit that re-forks the lineage fails"
risk: high
